{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-closed-immersion}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d47dc6ea4da56675f99c9bca3529e95b6e2f3a64fa8d5c84a7d6a24246200835", "source_text": "Closed immersions of locally ringed spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f8e41ea8ad07b439fa02163458795fea5e633e1ee2c83551b3e7a46c49f6958", "unit_id": "tag:01HJ:title"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-definition-closed-immersion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18389d47f1847cb5fdd080c7435f3ec716dbfce6e832df9b9477466d0377e230", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe follow our conventions introduced in\nModules, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c45a4efd213f9410ef7828c209e89cec873fec1a634dc2fff0fc70a18655a5ee", "unit_id": "tag:01HJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$i$", "MATH_0003": "$i$", "MATH_0004": "$Z$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\to i_*\\mathcal{O}_Z$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-closed-immersion-locally-ringed-spaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d16218b72af606d2ef54ff4bebe25b4363093e059339d8a1fcdd93f2d1b1a5d4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:610a92803b91145249aed4c3201e2eadd115d77dfd8bad38a38a4f23d729c3aa", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of locally ringed spaces.\nWe say that <MATH_0002> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>closed immersion<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The map <MATH_0003> is a homeomorphism of <MATH_0004> onto a closed subset of <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The map <MATH_0006> is surjective;\nlet <MATH_0007> denote the kernel.\n<STRUCT_0004> The <MATH_0008>-module <MATH_0009>\nis locally generated by sections.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a40bd909b6701db869be08a1bac2f4898c49d7305e818311a4c89a39821f3bee", "unit_id": "tag:01HK:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$f : f^{-1}U_i \\to U_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-closed-local-target}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f5d08f51154fd61ad0005933f8a14320c047de7dcde3dd45959b85ebb1147261", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3b9db702df29bf9443b091e254c2b015614f040d267b3bf5224c1dfe54c4b93", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of locally ringed spaces.\nIn order for <MATH_0002> to be a closed immersion it suffices\nthat there exists an open covering <MATH_0003> such\nthat each <MATH_0004> is a closed immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:058d2cf863cbcc366ceed443c1cb335dc7d4c6ffc0ff727487079ed5a9838b09", "unit_id": "tag:01HL:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:da688ccc327b3a7c27ec4f6eb6b9a74d35745d73f1d86126fb20079336be83c4", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:01HL:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "01HJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$Z$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X/\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_Z$", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$i_*\\mathcal{O}_Z = \\mathcal{O}_X/\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0011": "$z \\in Z$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{Z, z}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, i(z)}/\\mathcal{I}_{i(z)}$", "MATH_0014": "$i : (Z, \\mathcal{O}_Z) \\to (X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-support-sheaf-rings-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{modules-lemma-i-star-exact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-closed-subspace}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ba831fc270c5fa8afbe2387dac9ff9a2f68679015de0a896c4fed457b0aa9b4c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a3057e4edc3956cf8640278ee2eb8bee839aff7637c6c96daf813f9e067a8123", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally ringed space.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf\nof ideals which is locally generated by sections as a sheaf\nof <MATH_0003>-modules. Let <MATH_0004> be the support of\nthe sheaf of rings <MATH_0005>.\nThis is a closed subset of <MATH_0006>, by\nModules, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nDenote <MATH_0007> the inclusion map.\nBy Modules, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthere is a unique sheaf of rings <MATH_0008> on <MATH_0009>\nwith <MATH_0010>.\nFor any <MATH_0011> the stalk <MATH_0012>\nis equal to a quotient <MATH_0013>\nof a local ring and nonzero, hence a local ring.\nThus <MATH_0014> is\na closed immersion of locally ringed spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b8eb02ea04a942e43a3aad8f70971f42d60e60be09bdc051339a1a3e19381a1d", "unit_id": "tag:01HM:statement"}
